        "name": "Vellumis Excision",
        "system": {
          "actionType": {
            "value": "passive"
          },
          "actions": {
            "value": null
          },
          "category": "class",
          "description": {
            "value": "<p><strong>Access</strong> You're a member of the Vellumis Scholars.</p><hr /><p>You seek to excise the rot from the Gravelands and have made progress to do so. You can cast @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Field of Life] as a 6th-rank halcyon spell, and you gain a 6th-rank halcyon spell slot. When you cast your halcyon <em>field of life</em> as a primal spell, any living creatures in the area when you Sustain the spell gain a +2 status bonus to saving throws against curses, diseases, and poisons for 1 round.</p>\n<p>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.feat-effects.Item.Effect: Vellumis Excision]</p><hr /><p><strong>Special</strong> If you have the Halcyon Spellcasting Sage feat, you treat the <em>field of life</em> halcyon spell gained from this feat as a signature spell, even though halcyon spells normally can't be signature spells.</p>"
          },
          "level": {
            "value": 16
          },
          "prerequisites": {
            "value": [
              {
                "value": "Halcyon Spellcasting Adept"
              }
            ]
          },
          "publication": {
